WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.611
An AI proved

00:00:01.423 --> 00:00:02.555
this speedrun can

00:00:02.366 --> 00:00:03.392
never be beaten

00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:05.226
Speedrunners beat the

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.278
PICO-8 platformer Celeste

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:09.790
Classic in 2,843

00:00:09.602 --> 00:00:10.344
frames

00:00:10.484 --> 00:00:11.922
Harmonic's Aristotle

00:00:11.734 --> 00:00:12.629
proved no one

00:00:12.441 --> 00:00:13.243
will ever do

00:00:13.054 --> 00:00:13.643
better

00:00:14.182 --> 00:00:15.373
It translated the

00:00:15.184 --> 00:00:16.222
game into Lean

00:00:16.446 --> 00:00:17.908
a formal verification

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.380
language

00:00:18.545 --> 00:00:19.406
then pruned the

00:00:19.217 --> 00:00:19.901
search

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:20.924
In the hardest

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:21.525
room it checked

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:23.330
about 224 million

00:00:23.141 --> 00:00:23.766
states

00:00:23.955 --> 00:00:25.417
over 100 orders

00:00:25.229 --> 00:00:26.643
of magnitude fewer

00:00:26.455 --> 00:00:27.551
than brute force

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:28.978
In a one-dash

00:00:28.789 --> 00:00:29.626
category

00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:30.381
it beat the

00:00:30.193 --> 00:00:32.822
2,941-frame record

00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:35.369
with a 2,937-frame

00:00:35.181 --> 00:00:35.664
run

00:00:35.818 --> 00:00:36.843
and proved that

00:00:36.678 --> 00:00:37.692
optimal too

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:39.228
Full story on

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:39.935
the dashboard
